 renders correctly in PRINT position and renders a raw heap address
 everywhere else. LANGUAGE.md:3082-3085 says all sinks "share one name
 resolver" and render "identically whether the result is printed, written to
 a file, or built into a buffer"; LANGUAGE.md:3054-3056 says a format string
 used as a value "works as a text initializer or assignment". Neither holds
 for a collection.
 The address CHANGES BETWEEN RUNS, so this probe prints stable verdicts
 instead of the addresses; the raw values seen were
 139857342844928 / 139857342840832 / 139857342844928 in one run and
 different in the next. Found while probing LST-35; the claim lines are in
 the FMT ledger's range (2995-3138), not this one.
